{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "This trip's own trace shows no route deviation at all. POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km the governing measurement, and it records 19.76 km against a booked optimal of 19.6 km - an excess of 0.16 km, or 0.816% of optimal. Both establishment gates must pass and both fail by an order of magnitude: 0.16 km is far below the 0.8 km absolute threshold, and 0.816% is far below the 20% proportional threshold. Where either test fails, POL-RD-01 states that no deviation exists and the outcome is NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00506", "EV-TRIP-00506"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider carries the initial burden under POL-RD-08 and has not discharged its second limb. Limb (a) is satisfied - trip_id TRP-00506 matches across the trip record, the trace and the fare breakdown - but limb (b) requires an excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold, and the unimpaired trace yields 0.16 km / 0.816%. The burden therefore never shifts to the driver, and the driver needs no exculpatory clause, because there is no excess to excuse.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00506", "EV-GPS-00506", "EV-FARE-00506"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Every other artifact corroborates a direct, uninterrupted drive on the route the platform assigned. The trip record shows actual_duration_min 24.0 against optimal_duration_min 24.0 - parity to the tenth of a minute - with wait_time_min 1.0, no pickup amendment and no dropoff amendment, on a RYDE_XL vehicle. The trace covers 100% of the trip with 145 fixes, an empty gaps list and a maximum gap of 0 seconds. The billed distance (19.8 km) does not fall short of the trace (19.76 km), so no unbilled-distance question arises either.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00506", "EV-GPS-00506"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This is an UPFRONT_QUOTE trip with quoted_fare_sgd 45.00, so POL-RD-11 governs and POL-RD-02 does not run: the distance and time charges were fixed at booking and no distance-or-time refund is available to the rider however large the excess. The rider's remedy is confined to (a) the amount by which charged_total exceeds the quote plus any properly chargeable pass-through line, and (b) a POL-RD-09 correction - and here the pass-throughs are nil: erp_gantries is empty, the airport surcharge line is 0.00 (this trip ENDS at Changi T3, it does not originate there), and the waiting fee is 0.00. On the platform's own arithmetic the over-quote differential is 10.20, so the 55.20 the rider contests is unreachable in any event, and no part of that differential is attributable to a deviation or to the driver's driving.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00506", "EV-GPS-00506"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.charged_over_quote",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No rider instruction of any kind is on the record. The in-app chat log for this trip contains zero messages and no timestamps, so there is no POL-RD-04 detour request, no named stop and no named road - and equally no in-trip complaint about the route. The driver drove the route the app gave him, and the only route measurement in the bundle is the trace showing 0.82% variation from optimal.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00506", "EV-GPS-00506"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing in the driver's record supports an adverse finding against him. POL-RD-06 is not even engaged, because it is consulted only on a MATERIAL deviation and 0.16 km is nowhere near the materiality gate of 8.0 km or 50% of optimal. Were it consulted, driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 250, so no pattern is established, no FULL_REFUND uplift follows and no conduct referral is warranted. The remaining profile fields - rating, acceptance rate, account age, lifetime trips - are context only under POL-GEN-01 and can never ground a finding.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00506"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.thresholds.material_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is clean for policy purposes and the case is decidable on the present record. POL-RD-07's impairment limbs do not fire: 145 fixes at a 10-second cadence, coverage 100%, an empty gaps list, max_gap_sec 0.0, no straight-line jump above 500 m and no sampling interval above 30 seconds. POL-RD-10(3) therefore has no trigger, so the route question can be settled now rather than held for a human reviewer.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00506"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I disclose an impaired artifact: EV-ADVIS-00506-01 is the traffic advisory and it carries admissibility status MISSING, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT and weight_multiplier 0.0 with no payload, because no advisory covers the PIE eastbound in this window. Its effect is neutral here. POL-RD-03 exoneration needs an advisory naming a segment the optimal route traverses, and POL-RD-13 tests only a traffic excuse a party actually asserts - the driver asserts none. The booked optimal of 19.6 km therefore remains the only baseline in the record, and no closure adjustment changes the measured excess.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00506-01", "EV-TRIP-00506"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-13", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On this rider-filed dispute the present state is payment_status CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00, and POL-GEN-03 makes NO_ACTION party-relative: it leaves that state as it is. Because no deviation exists, no distance-or-time refund runs on an upfront-quoted trip, and no chargeable pass-through line is present, the rider's route claim is not supported by this trip's evidence and no adverse finding, uplift or conduct referral should issue against the driver. To the extent the fare model produced any differential, that is a platform billing computation on the rider's own account, not a route finding against the man who drove the app's route.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00506", "EV-GPS-00506"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 10.2,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute is really about the fare, not the road, and the money moves on the fare question.\n\nTHE ROUTE. The GPS trace for TRP-00506 measures 19.76 km against a booked optimal of 19.6 km — an excess of 0.16 km, or 0.82%. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only when the excess is above both 0.8 km and 20% of optimal; neither gate is remotely met (the trace figure governs over the trip record's rounded 19.8 km copy). No route deviation exists, so nothing said about the driver's driving is upheld against him, no POL-RD-06 repeat-deviation check is engaged (0.16 km is nowhere near the 8.0 km / 50% materiality gate, and in any event deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 250), and no conduct referral issues. No POL-RD-04 driver compensation arises either: the billed distance (19.8 km) does not fall short of the trace, so there is no unbilled distance to compensate. The driver's submission that no adverse route finding should issue against him is ACCEPTED.\n\nTHE FARE. The trip was booked on an UPFRONT_QUOTE with a locked fare of SGD 45.00, and SGD 55.20 was charged. POL-RD-11(a) refunds the amount by which charged_total exceeds the locked quote plus any properly chargeable pass-through line. The fare breakdown itemises no ERP (erp_lines empty, 0.00), no airport surcharge (0.00, which is correct because this trip ENDS at Changi T3 and does not originate there) and no waiting-time fee (0.00), so properly chargeable is 0.00 and the refund is 55.20 − 45.00 − 0.00 = SGD 10.20. POL-RD-02 does not run on an upfront-quoted trip, so the distance and time charges are not recomputed and the rider recovers nothing on those lines; the SGD 10.20 is the whole of the relief, not the SGD 55.20 contested. The driver's own filing concedes the 10.20 over-quote differential on the platform's arithmetic; his submission that the outcome should be NO_ACTION is therefore accepted only so far as it concerns him — no money moves against him — and rejected as to the rider, because POL-GEN-03's NO_ACTION preserves the present state and the present state is a charge of 55.20 of which 10.20 was never properly chargeable.\n\nCONFIDENCE AND ESCALATION. The deciding figures sit on EV-FARE-00506 at weight 1.0, and the no-deviation finding sits on EV-GPS-00506 and EV-TRIP-00506, both at weight 1.0; the trace is complete (145 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, empty gaps list, max gap 0 s) and clean under POL-RD-07(a)–(c). Trip identifiers and timestamps match across the artifacts, and no charge line lacks a counterpart. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires, so the case is decided rather than held. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00506-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0, but no party asserts a traffic cause (the driver expressly says he drove the route the app gave) and neither advocate relies on it as an exculpatory record, so it decides nothing; under POL-RD-13 its absence is a gap in the bundle, not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation. No clause produces a referral on these facts.\n\nNET RESULT. The rider is refunded SGD 10.20 of the SGD 55.20 contested; the rest of the charge stands as the amount properly chargeable above the locked quote. The driver owes nothing and is owed nothing.",
    "referrals": []
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

