    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider — you are right about the money, but not about the route. Your own trip trace (EV-GPS-00506) records 19.76 km driven against a booked optimal of 19.6 km: an excess of 0.16 km, or 0.82%. POL-RD-01 requires an excess greater than 0.8 km AND greater than 20% before any deviation is established; both gates fail by an order of magnitude, so no route deviation exists, no POL-RD-02 recomputation runs, and nothing issues against the driver. The money finding is separate and it is yours. This trip was booked as an UPFRONT_QUOTE at SGD 45.00 (fare_breakdown.quoted_fare_sgd on EV-FARE-00506) and you were charged SGD 55.20. Nothing beyond the quote was properly chargeable: erp_lines is empty (SGD 0.00), the airport surcharge is SGD 0.00 (the trip ENDS at Changi Terminal 3; a trip that ends at an airport carries no surcharge), and the waiting fee is SGD 0.00 — so properly_chargeable.total is SGD 0.00. Under POL-RD-11(a) the SGD 10.20 by which charged_total exceeds the locked quote plus those lines is refunded in full; rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 it remains SGD 10.20. That is a PARTIAL_REFUND of the SGD 55.20 you contested, leaving the charge standing only in its reduced form.\n\nTo the driver — your account is accepted and no adverse finding issues against you. You drove the route the app gave you: the trace covers 100% of the trip with 145 fixes at a 10-second cadence, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0, and a measured excess of 0.16 km over the booked optimal. The in-app chat log for this trip holds zero messages, so there is no rider instruction to detour and no in-trip complaint about your driving. POL-RD-06 is not engaged — its materiality gate (8.0 km or 50%) is nowhere near 0.16 km — and driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 250 completed trips, so no pattern, no FULL_REFUND uplift and no conduct referral. POL-RD-04's unbilled-distance limb does not arise either, because the billed distance (19.8 km) is not short of the trace (19.76 km). Your conclusion that this is NO_ACTION does not follow, however: on an upfront-quoted trip POL-RD-11(a) refunds the amount charged over the locked quote whether or not a deviation exists, and the SGD 10.20 gap is accounted for by no distance, time, ERP, surcharge or waiting line. POL-RD-01's default speaks to the deviation question; it does not extinguish the POL-RD-11 remedy that the fare ledger itself publishes as available. Your point that no part of the differential is attributable to a deviation or to your driving is accepted.\n\nOn the traffic advisory. EV-ADVIS-00506-01 is MISSING, with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — no advisory covers the PIE eastbound in this window. No party asserted an external traffic cause, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and nothing turns on it: the advisory is cited only for its absence, it carries no fact in either direction, and it neither exonerates under POL-RD-03 nor escalates under POL-RD-10(5) (POL-RD-13(1)). No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the trip identifier TRP-00506 matches across trip record, trace and fare breakdown; the trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a)–(c); the refund is far below SGD 150 and below charged_total; and every charged line corresponds to the trace and trip record.\n\nConfidence is 0.90. Every artifact carrying a deciding fact — EV-FARE-00506 (quoted fare, charged total and pass-through lines), EV-GPS-00506 and EV-TRIP-00506 (the no-deviation finding) — is at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0; the MISSING advisory at 0.0 carries no fact and does not lower it. No referral is produced: POL-RD-06(c) is not engaged (no material deviation, no pattern) and POL-RD-09(4) is not engaged (no unmatched gantry and no wrongly applied surcharge)."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

