    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the route complaint fails, but the bill does not stand, and the two questions are decided separately.\n\nTHE ROUTE. Both advocates read the trace the same way and so do I. EV-GPS-00506 (weight 1.0) records trace_distance_km 19.76 against the booked optimal of 19.6 km on EV-TRIP-00506 — an excess of 0.16 km, or 0.82%. POL-RD-01 requires BOTH gates to pass: more than 0.8 km absolute AND more than 20% of optimal. Both fail by an order of magnitude, so no deviation is established, no POL-RD-02 recomputation runs, no materiality review under POL-RD-06 arises, and nothing adverse attaches to the driver. The driver's account — he drove the route the app gave him — is consistent with the trace: 145 fixes, 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, an empty gaps list and a maximum gap of 0 seconds. There is no chat instruction either (EV-CHAT-00506 contains zero messages), so no POL-RD-04 question exists.\n\nTHE MONEY. This is an UPFRONT_QUOTE trip: EV-FARE-00506 (weight 1.0) records fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE and quoted_fare_sgd 45.00. POL-RD-11 therefore governs and POL-RD-02 does not run — no distance-or-time refund is available however large the excess. POL-RD-11(a) gives the rider the amount by which charged_total exceeds the locked quote, less the pass-through and statutory lines properly chargeable under POL-RD-09. Charged_total is 55.20; the quote is 45.00; the differential is 10.20. Every pass-through line is nil: no ERP gantries (0.00), airport surcharge 0.00 (this trip ENDS at Changi T3, so no surcharge is chargeable and none was added), waiting-time fee 0.00 — properly_chargeable.total 0.00. So 55.20 − 45.00 − 0.00 = 10.20, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 is 10.20. That is also the ledger's own published figure (pol_rd_11_remedy 10.20, pol_rd_11_remedy_available true).\n\nTHE DRIVER'S ANSWER ON THE MONEY. The driver's submission that no deviation exists is accepted in full, and so is his arithmetic (he too reaches 10.20 as the over-quote differential). His conclusion of NO_ACTION is rejected. POL-RD-01's default governs deviation claims; it does not extinguish POL-RD-11(a), which is a standalone remedy for a trip priced on a locked quote and is available on its own terms. Under POL-RD-11 the distance-and-time loss on an upfront trip falls on the platform, not on the rider, so the excess over the quote cannot simply be kept, and it is not recoverable from the driver either. No driver compensation is due: the billed distance of 19.8 km does not fall short of the trace's 19.76 km, so the POL-RD-04 unbilled-distance limb has nothing behind it.\n\nNO ESCALATION, NO REFERRAL. The trace is unimpaired for POL-RD-07 purposes (limbs (a)–(c) do not fire), so POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged; trip identifiers match across all three instruments; no timestamps conflict; the refund is far below SGD 150 and well below charged_total; and no party asserts an external traffic cause. EV-ADVIS-00506-01 (TRAFFIC_ADVISORY, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT — no advisory covers the PIE eastbound in this window) is citable for its absence only and carries no fact; because no party invoked it as an exculpatory ground, its absence is a gap in the bundle rather than a POL-RD-10(5) contradiction (POL-RD-13(1)). The deciding facts sit on EV-FARE-00506, EV-GPS-00506 and EV-TRIP-00506, each at weight_multiplier 1.0, so confidence is not capped and the 0.70 floor is not approached. No clause produces a referral: POL-RD-06(c) needs an established repeat pattern and a material deviation, and here deviation_flags_90d is 0 over completed_trips_90d 250, while 0.16 km is nowhere near the materiality gate; POL-RD-09(4) is not engaged because no gantry line and no airport surcharge were wrongly charged.\n\nOUTCOME. Payment status is CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so the 10.20 now comes off the filing rider's bill as a PARTIAL_REFUND of the 55.20 contested. The charge is otherwise undisturbed and no finding is made against the driver.",
